# ── Rust ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Note: Cargo.lock IS committed for binaries (this is a binary crate).
# Do not ignore it — it pins dependency versions for reproducible builds.

# ── Cushion ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: .cushion.toml and .cushion/ledger.jsonl SHOULD be committed.
# The ledger is the shared team budget — committing it makes the cushion
# tamper-evident across the whole team and prevents local "refunds".
#
# However, during development of Cushion itself, local runs of `cushion
# demo` or `cushion check` create throwaway state. Those are ignored below
# only if you run the tool in its own repo during development.
#
# If you use Cushion ON its own repo while developing, uncomment:
# /.cushion/
# /.cushion.toml

# Temp files created by `cushion ui` or crash recovery
.cushion/*.tmp
.cushion/*.swp

# ── Environment & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*

# ── Editors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VS Code
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example

# JetBrains / IntelliJ / RustRover
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Vim / Neovim
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.*.sw?
Session.vim
.netrwhist

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# Sublime
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# Helix
.helix/

# Zed
.zed/

